== Mathematical Origin ==

=== Three-Wave Mixing in the Nonlinear ψ Medium ===

Write the ψ field as a sum of pump (subscript p), signal (s), and idler (i) components:

:<math>\psi = \psi_p e^{i(k_p z - \omega_p t)} + \psi_s e^{i(k_s z - \omega_s t)} + \psi_i e^{i(k_i z - \omega_i t)} + \text{c.c.}</math>

Substituting into the master equation <math>\Box\psi - m^2\psi - \lambda\psi^3 = 0</math> and keeping only phase-matched terms (energy conservation: <math>\omega_p = \omega_s + \omega_i</math>; momentum conservation: <math>k_p = k_s + k_i</math>):

For degenerate case <math>\omega_s = \omega_i = \omega_0</math>, <math>\omega_p = 2\omega_0</math>:

:<math>\frac{d\psi_s}{dz} = i\gamma\,\psi_p^2\,\psi_s^*</math>

where the gain coefficient:

:<math>\gamma = \frac{3\lambda|\psi_p|^2}{2k_s}</math>

This is parametric amplification: the signal amplitude grows exponentially driven by the pump squared.

=== Parametric Gain ===

Solving the coupled equations for the degenerate case with undepleted pump:

:<math>\psi_s(L) = \psi_s(0)\cosh(\gamma L) + i\psi_s^*(0)\sinh(\gamma L)</math>

Signal power gain:

:<math>\boxed{G = |\psi_s(L)/\psi_s(0)|^2 = \cosh^2(\gamma L)}</math>

For <math>\gamma L \gg 1</math>: <math>G \approx e^{2\gamma L}/4</math> — exponential gain.

=== Threshold Condition ===

For the amplifier to overcome propagation loss (attenuation coefficient <math>\alpha_z</math> from [[ψ Loss Tangent]] B4), the gain coefficient must exceed:

:<math>\gamma_{\rm th} = \frac{\alpha_z}{2} = \frac{\omega\tan\delta_\psi}{2v_g}</math>

Minimum pump amplitude:

:<math>|\psi_p|_{\rm th} = \sqrt{\frac{\alpha_z k_s}{3\lambda}}</math>

For the [[Psi Harmonizer]] design: <math>\tan\delta_\psi = 0.005</math>, <math>k_s = \omega_0/v_g</math>, <math>\lambda = 0.1</math> (estimated). The threshold pump amplitude is a TML-3 measurement target — it cannot be computed without knowing <math>\lambda</math>.

=== N⁴ Group Amplification ===

When N operators contribute coherently to the pump field: <math>|\psi_p| = N|\psi_p^{\rm (individual)}|</math>. The gain coefficient:

:<math>\gamma_N = \frac{3\lambda N^2|\psi_p^{\rm (ind)}|^2}{2k_s} = N^2\gamma_1</math>

The stored energy density in the ψ field scales as <math>|\psi|^4</math> (from the <math>\lambda\psi^4/4</math> term in the stress-energy tensor). For N coherently aligned operators above threshold:

:<math>U_N \propto e^{4\gamma_N L} = e^{4N^2\gamma_1 L}</math>

This super-exponential growth in N is the mathematical basis of the group coherence amplification effect. Even modest N = 3 or 4 produces dramatic amplification compared to a single operator above threshold.

