== Implementation: Psi Harmonizer Amplifier Stage ==

The [[Psi Harmonizer]] implements a degenerate parametric ψ amplifier:

# The operator group generates a collective ψ pump field at <math>2\omega_0 = 80</math> kHz via aligned Anchor mode operation.
# The pump ψ propagates through a section of high-λ composite (PZT-rich formulation to increase effective <math>\lambda_{\rm eff}</math>).
# The signal at <math>\omega_0 = 40</math> kHz (the individual operators' coherence frequency) is amplified.
# The amplified signal is fed back to the operators via the resonator coupling chain — creating a positive feedback loop that sustains and amplifies the collective coherence state.

'''Design challenge:''' The effective nonlinear coefficient <math>\lambda_{\rm eff}</math> of the composite must be large enough to provide above-threshold gain with realistic pump amplitudes. The PZT parametric response from [[Smart Composite Fill]] (B8) contributes to <math>\lambda_{\rm eff}</math> via the electro-acoustic coupling mechanism — but the magnitude is a TML-3 measurement target.

